[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4524851761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119679#issuecomment-4524851761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119679","id":4524851761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDbPCMQ","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T08:38:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T08:38:17Z","body":"> I am quite bothered by the blurriness though.\r\n\r\nCurrently, oversampling is not affected by canvas item scale, only by viewport settings. So it probably will need to use `SubViewport` + `SubViewportContainer` with set oversampling to be fully sharp.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4524851761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525570447","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119679#issuecomment-4525570447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119679","id":4525570447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDb65jw","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T13:59:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T13:59:15Z","body":"I tried implementing it with a `SubViewport`, but that brings its own set of problems. Besides, we have a whole internal system in place for theme contexts in order to not need viewport hackery.\r\n\r\nI think the best approach would be that, in the future, we make oversampling take scaling into account. Would that be possible, @bruvzg?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525570447/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525576470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119679#issuecomment-4525576470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119679","id":4525576470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDb7RFg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T14:01:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T14:01:53Z","body":"> I think the best approach would be that, in the future, we make oversampling take scaling into account.\r\n\r\nIt should be possible, and probably pretty easy to implement, as long as it is optional, since it not always useful and can create a lot of overhead if automatically applied to everything.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525576470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525580674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119679#issuecomment-4525580674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119679","id":4525580674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDb7hgg","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id